{"ref":"BDB, הֵיךְ","hw":"הֵיךְ","html":"† <big><big><span dir=\"rtl\">הֵיךְ</span></big></big>  <strong>adv. how</strong>? <strong>(</strong><span dir=\"rtl\">היך</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܗܝܟ</span>, <em>id.</em>, in Palest. Aramaic, as <a data-ref=\"Job 21:34\" href=\"/Job.21.34\">Jb 21:34</a> 𝔗, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 3:9\" href=\"/Genesis.3.9\">Gn 3:9</a> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 1:12\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.1.12\">Dt 1:12</a> 𝔗<sup>Ps.-J.</sup>, Mat 22:12 𝔖<sup>Jerus.</sup> (though usually these words have the force of <em>as</em>), and in <span dir=\"rtl\">הֵיכְדֵין</span> <em>how, then?</em> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 73:11\" href=\"/Psalms.73.11\">ψ 73:11</a> + 𝔗; cf. Bevan<sup>Dan p. 29</sup><strong>)</strong>—only twice, in late Heb., <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 13:12\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.13.12\">1 Ch 13:12</a> (‖ <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 6:9\" href=\"/II_Samuel.6.9\">2 S 6:9</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">אֵיךְ</span>), <a data-ref=\"Daniel 10:17\" href=\"/Daniel.10.17\">Dan 10:17</a>.","next":"BDB, הֵיכָל","prev":"BDB, הַיָּה²"}